{"link":{"rel":"self","url":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/catalog/item/6a8490171ba49b3133cd8055"},"relatedItems":{"link":{"url":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/catalog/itemLinks?itemId=6a8490171ba49b3133cd8055","rel":"related"}},"id":"6a8490171ba49b3133cd8055","identifiers":[{"type":"IPDS","scheme":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/vocab/category/item/identifier","key":"IP-192838"},{"type":"DOI","scheme":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/vocab/category/item/identifier","key":"doi:10.5066/P1KEQASH"},{"type":"USGS_keywords","scheme":"https://www.sciencebase.gov/vocab/category/item/identifier","key":"Economic Geology, Mineral Resources"}],"title":"2024 Minerals Yearbook, volume III, Area Reports — International: country reports, global production, and global mineral facilities","summary":"The U.S. Geological Survey's Minerals Yearbook Volume III: Area Reports — International publication provides an annual review of the mineral and materials industries of over 150 countries worldwide. This volume of work includes individual country reports that examine the performance and developments of a country's mineral industry that occurred during a given year. Topics covered in each country report may include mineral production and trade, government policies and programs, industry structure, and developments in the commodity sector. Tabular data include mineral commodity production statistics over a 5-year period and a summary of mineral facilities including annual production capacities, where data are available. The 2024 Minerals [...]","body":"The U.S. Geological Survey's Minerals Yearbook Volume III: Area Reports — International publication provides an annual review of the mineral and materials industries of over 150 countries worldwide. This volume of work includes individual country reports that examine the performance and developments of a country's mineral industry that occurred during a given year. Topics covered in each country report may include mineral production and trade, government policies and programs, industry structure, and developments in the commodity sector. Tabular data include mineral commodity production statistics over a 5-year period and a summary of mineral facilities including annual production capacities, where data are available. The 2024 Minerals Yearbook Volume III: Area Reports — International data release provides a compilation of the Minerals Yearbook country reports discussing information, events, data, and statistics for the year 2024, mineral commodity production data for the years 2020 through 2024, and country-level mineral facilities data. Country reports are compiled into a .txt file and tabular data are provided in .csv format in this data release.","citation":"National Minerals Information Center (NMIC), 2026, 2024 Minerals Yearbook, volume III, Area Reports — International: country reports, global production, and global mineral facilities: U.S. Geological Survey data release, https://doi.org/10.5066/P1KEQASH.","purpose":"This data release includes country-by-country mineral commodity production statistics for the years 2020 through 2024 as well as locations and production capacities of mineral facilities at yearend 2024. These data accompany the 2024 country reports in the U.S. Geological Survey's Minerals Yearbook Volume III: Area Reports — International (https://doi.org/10.3133/mybvIII); these reports analyze the importance of minerals to the economies of over 150 nations and the United States. Production and facility data are provided in a .csv format and country reports are provided in a .txt file.","rights":"This work is marked with the Creative Commons Zero v1.0 Universal (CC0-1.0) public domain dedication; https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/. These data are marked with a Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal License. These data are in the public domain and do not have any use constraints. The U.S. Geological Survey (USGS) provides these data \"as is.\" Unless otherwise stated, all data and metadata are considered to satisfy the quality standards relative to the purpose for which the data were collected. Although these data and associated metadata have been processed successfully on USGS computer systems, reviewed for accuracy and completeness, and approved for release by the USGS, no warranty expressed or implied is made regarding the display or utility of the data on any other system or for general or scientific purposes, nor shall the act of distribution constitute any such warranty. The burden for determining fitness for use of these data lies entirely with the user. Users are advised to read the dataset's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.\n    ","provenance":{"dateCreated":"2026-08-18T17:02:15Z","lastUpdated":"2026-08-31T18:42:50Z"},"maintenanceUpdateFrequency":"None planned","hasChildren":false,"parentId":"5c8c03e4e4b0938824529f7d","contacts":[{"name":"National Minerals Information Center","oldPartyId":17231,"type":"SDC Data Owner","contactType":"organization","onlineResource":"https://www.usgs.gov/centers/nmic","active":true,"aliases":["MINERALS INFORMATION TEAM","MINERALS INFO TEAM","NATIONAL MINERALS INFORMATION CTR"],"organization":{},"primaryLocation":{"shortName":"DFC, Bldg 20, KAC","name":"Denver Federal Center - DFC Bldg 20 [KAC]","building":"DFC Bldg 20","buildingCode":"KAC","latitude":39.71916667,"longitude":-105.1143417,"streetAddress":{"line1":"West 6th Ave. & Kipling St.","line2":"DFC Bldg. 20","city":"Lakewood","state":"CO","zip":"80225-0046","country":"USA"},"mailAddress":{"line1":"Box 25046","line2":"Mailstop 911","city":"Denver","state":"CO","zip":"80225-0046","country":"USA"}}},{"name":"Geology, Energy, and Minerals","oldPartyId":64232,"type":"USGS Mission Area","contactType":"organization","active":true,"organization":{"directoryId":"64232","displayText":"Energy and Minerals"},"primaryLocation":{"streetAddress":{},"mailAddress":{}}},{"name":"National Minerals Information Center","type":"Poin